<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:cf="using:Cornflower.Controls"
                    xmlns:wp81="using:Cornflower.Themes.Wp81">
  <!--
    The Windows Phone 8.1 ListView and ListViewItem, on Avalonia's ListBox and ListBoxItem: the default styles of the
    8.1 Update 1 runtime (listview.json and listviewitem.json, which equal the SDK's generic.xaml), re-expressed as
    Avalonia ControlThemes. Every value is the phone's resource key, by DynamicResource, so it follows the theme
    variant and an app can override it by its key, but for the check mode's two offsets (below).
    docs/controls/ListView/PLAN.md has the values and their sources.

    The ListView's look is the ListBox's own: the list 8.1 apps write is a ListView, and the phone's ListBox, kept for
    8.0's apps, is a later tier's, which can take a key of its own.

    ListView: the phone's Border round a ScrollViewer round an ItemsPresenter. The ScrollViewer is a plain one, the
    phone's with its thin indicators (Controls/ScrollViewer.axaml), named as Avalonia's ListBox looks for it, its
    values bound from the ListBox's attached ScrollViewer values as the phone's are (docs/controls/ScrollViewer,
    "How a later control holds it"). The phone's ItemsStackPanel is Avalonia's VirtualizingStackPanel.

    ListViewItem, part for part, with Avalonia's PART_ContentPresenter for the phone's contentPresenter:
    - OuterContainer, untilted; ReorderHintContent, its Grid, with a transparent background, takes the hits across
      the item, so a press at its very edge still selects (as the Button's Root).
    - CheckboxTiltContainer, at the top left inside ListViewItemMultiselectCheckBoxMargin, holds the check box: a
      25.5 Rectangle in CheckBox's brushes and the tick (Wp81.Glyph.CheckMark at its own size, as CheckBox's), in
      CheckboxContainer, which sits 40.5 to the left, clipped away by CheckboxOuterContainer's 25.5 square, until the
      list is in the check mode.
    - ContentContainer and TiltContainer, the part the phone's PointerDownThemeAnimation targets, so it is marked
      Tilt.IsTarget: the whole content tilts, the check box doesn't; ContentBorder draws the item's Background,
      BorderBrush and BorderThickness, and slides 40.5 to the right in the check mode.
    - SelectedBorder at nought opacity, round SelectedCheckMark, the earmark (Wp81.Glyph.SelectedEarmark) and its tick
      (Wp81.Glyph.CheckMark stretched to 17 x 14.5), which Selected shows: a ListView item never shows them, as
      SelectedBorder shows only in GridMultiSelect, a GridView's state (Wp81GridViewItemTheme, at the end of this file), but they make an item
      at least 2.5 + 34 + 2.5 tall, 39.17 once laid out at 2.4, as the phone's are.
    - Left out: the placeholder TextBlock and Rectangle (DataPlaceholder: Avalonia has no data virtualisation), the
      ScaleTransform and the reorder states (reorder is deferred).

    The visual states: Pressed (Avalonia's :pressed, at once on a press, as the phone's) runs the tilt on
    TiltContainer, in the check mode too; CheckboxPressed, a press on the box in the check mode
    (wp81:PhoneListMultiSelect.IsBoxPressed), fills the box with the accent and draws the tick over it, and
    PhoneListMultiSelect tilts the box alone, with no return. Disabled dims the content to ListViewItemDisabledThemeOpacity (the 8.1
    Update 1 runtime's 0.4), the box and tick to their disabled brushes, and the selected parts to Transparent.
    Selected (:selected) shows the tick, which shows only in the check mode, and SelectedCheckMark. ListMultiSelect is wp81:PhoneListMultiSelect.IsOn, which the ListView theme sets
    on a list whose SelectionMode has Multiple and Toggle (WinRT's Multiple; Multiple alone, its Extended, the phone
    shows with no boxes), and its items inherit: the box comes in and the content goes over, both over
    the phone's 0.15 s, linear. Its two offsets are ListViewItemContentOffsetX (-40.5) and
    ListViewItemContentTranslateX (40.5), written here as literals: a transform transition takes a TransformOperations,
    which a resource double can't make. PointerOver, focus and SelectedUnfocused change nothing; FocusAdorner is
    cleared.
  -->

  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ListBox}" TargetType="ListBox">
    <Setter Property="IsTabStop" Value="False" />
    <Setter Property="KeyboardNavigation.TabNavigation" Value="Once" />
    <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility" Value="Disabled" />
    <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility" Value="Auto" />
    <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.IsDeferredScrollingEnabled" Value="False" />
    <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.BringIntoViewOnFocusChange" Value="True" />
    <!-- Not set by the phone's style: what its ListView inherits from the page. -->
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource PhoneForegroundBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="FocusAdorner" Value="{x:Null}" />
    <!-- Out of the check mode, unless the style below says so: set, not inherited, so a list in an item of a list in the
         check mode has its own. -->
    <Setter Property="wp81:PhoneListMultiSelect.IsOn" Value="False" />
    <Setter Property="ItemsPanel">
      <ItemsPanelTemplate>
        <VirtualizingStackPanel />
      </ItemsPanelTemplate>
    </Setter>
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <Border BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}">
          <ScrollViewer x:Name="PART_ScrollViewer"
                        HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility)}"
                        VerticalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility)}"
                        IsScrollChainingEnabled="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.IsScrollChainingEnabled)}"
                        IsDeferredScrollingEnabled="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.IsDeferredScrollingEnabled)}"
                        BringIntoViewOnFocusChange="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.BringIntoViewOnFocusChange)}"
                        AllowAutoHide="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.AllowAutoHide)}"
                        IsScrollInertiaEnabled="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.IsScrollInertiaEnabled)}"
                        HorizontalSnapPointsType="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.HorizontalSnapPointsType)}"
                        VerticalSnapPointsType="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.VerticalSnapPointsType)}">
            <Panel>
              <ItemsPresenter x:Name="PART_ItemsPresenter"
                              ItemsPanel="{TemplateBinding ItemsPanel}"
                              Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                              HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              VerticalAlignment="Top" />
              <!-- A grouped list's pinned header (cf:ListBoxOptions.GroupedItemsSource): ListBoxOptions puts a
                   cf:ListViewHeaderItem in it, and shows it at the viewport's top, in a vertical stack, as the phone's
                   ItemsStackPanel pins its group's header; never in the GridView's WrapPanel. Inside the ScrollViewer, so
                   the viewport clips it, a pan or the wheel on it scrolls the list, and the indicator draws over it. Over
                   the page's brush, so the items going under it don't show through, as on the phone. -->
              <Border x:Name="PART_StickyHeader"
                      IsVisible="False"
                      VerticalAlignment="Top"
                      Background="{DynamicResource ApplicationPageBackgroundThemeBrush}" />
            </Panel>
          </ScrollViewer>
        </Border>
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>

    <!--
      The check mode, WinRT's Multiple: Multiple (1) with Toggle (2), with or without AlwaysSelected (4), by value, as a
      selector's comma can't sit in a flags value. Multiple alone is WinRT's Extended, which the phone shows with no
      boxes. Its items inherit it.
    -->
    <Style Selector="^[SelectionMode=3], ^[SelectionMode=7]">
      <Setter Property="wp81:PhoneListMultiSelect.IsOn" Value="True" />
    </Style>
  </ControlTheme>

  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ListBoxItem}" TargetType="ListBoxItem">
    <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{DynamicResource ContentControlThemeFontFamily}" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource ControlContentThemeFontSize}" />
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
    <Setter Property="KeyboardNavigation.TabNavigation" Value="Local" />
    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="{DynamicResource ListViewItemMargin}" />
    <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left" />
    <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Top" />
    <Setter Property="FocusAdorner" Value="{x:Null}" />
    <!-- Not set by the phone's style: WinRT's own default, which Avalonia's ContentControl's is not. The tilted content
         draws past the item's edges, as the phone's does, and the check box's own clip hides it at rest. -->
    <Setter Property="ClipToBounds" Value="False" />
    <Setter Property="cf:Tilt.IsEnabled" Value="True" />
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <Border x:Name="OuterContainer">
          <Grid x:Name="ReorderHintContent" Background="Transparent">
            <Border x:Name="CheckboxTiltContainer"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                    VerticalAlignment="Top"
                    Margin="{DynamicResource ListViewItemMultiselectCheckBoxMargin}">
              <Border x:Name="CheckboxOuterContainer">
                <Border.Clip>
                  <RectangleGeometry Rect="0,0,25.5,25.5" />
                </Border.Clip>
                <Grid x:Name="CheckboxContainer" RenderTransform="translateX(-40.5px)" wp81:PhoneTransitions.Area="Control">
                  <Grid.Transitions>
                    <Transitions>
                      <TransformOperationsTransition Property="RenderTransform" Duration="0:0:0.15" />
                    </Transitions>
                  </Grid.Transitions>
                  <Rectangle x:Name="NormalRectangle"
                             Width="25.5"
                             Height="25.5"
                             Fill="{DynamicResource CheckBoxBackgroundThemeBrush}"
                             Stroke="{DynamicResource CheckBoxBorderThemeBrush}"
                             StrokeThickness="{DynamicResource CheckBoxBorderThemeThickness}" />
                  <Path x:Name="CheckGlyph"
                        IsHitTestVisible="False"
                        Opacity="0"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Fill="{DynamicResource CheckBoxForegroundThemeBrush}"
                        Data="{DynamicResource Wp81.Glyph.CheckMark}" />
                </Grid>
              </Border>
            </Border>
            <Border x:Name="ContentContainer">
              <Border x:Name="TiltContainer" cf:Tilt.IsTarget="True">
                <Border x:Name="ContentBorder"
                        Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                        BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                        RenderTransform="none"
                        wp81:PhoneTransitions.Area="Control">
                  <Border.Transitions>
                    <Transitions>
                      <TransformOperationsTransition Property="RenderTransform" Duration="0:0:0.15" />
                    </Transitions>
                  </Border.Transitions>
                  <ContentPresenter x:Name="PART_ContentPresenter"
                                    Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                    VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                                    Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                    ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                                    wp81:PhoneHeaderLine.IsEnabled="True" />
                </Border>
              </Border>
            </Border>
            <Border x:Name="SelectedBorder"
                    IsHitTestVisible="False"
                    Opacity="0"
                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource ListViewItemSelectedBackgroundThemeBrush}"
                    BorderThickness="{DynamicResource GridViewItemMultiselectBorderThickness}">
              <Grid x:Name="SelectedCheckMark"
                    Opacity="0"
                    Width="34"
                    Height="34"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                    VerticalAlignment="Top">
                <Path x:Name="SelectedEarmark"
                      Stretch="Fill"
                      Fill="{DynamicResource ListViewItemSelectedBackgroundThemeBrush}"
                      Data="{DynamicResource Wp81.Glyph.SelectedEarmark}" />
                <Path x:Name="SelectedGlyph"
                      Width="17"
                      Height="14.5"
                      Margin="0,1,1,0"
                      HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                      VerticalAlignment="Top"
                      Stretch="Fill"
                      Fill="{DynamicResource ListViewItemCheckThemeBrush}"
                      Data="{DynamicResource Wp81.Glyph.CheckMark}" />
              </Grid>
            </Border>
          </Grid>
        </Border>
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>

    <!-- Selected: the tick, and SelectedCheckMark, which shows only inside SelectedBorder, in a GridView's GridMultiSelect. -->
    <Style Selector="^:selected">
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Path#CheckGlyph">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Grid#SelectedCheckMark">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1" />
      </Style>
    </Style>

    <!-- ListMultiSelect: the box comes in and the content goes over. A press off the box is Pressed, the content's tilt. -->
    <Style Selector="^[(wp81|PhoneListMultiSelect.IsOn)=True]">
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Grid#CheckboxContainer">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateX(0px)" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#ContentBorder">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateX(40.5px)" />
      </Style>
    </Style>

    <!-- CheckboxPressed, a press on the box in the check mode: the accent box and the tick over it; PhoneListMultiSelect
         tilts the box. -->
    <Style Selector="^[(wp81|PhoneListMultiSelect.IsBoxPressed)=True]">
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Rectangle#NormalRectangle">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource CheckBoxPressedBackgroundThemeBrush}" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Path#CheckGlyph">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource CheckBoxPressedForegroundThemeBrush}" />
      </Style>
    </Style>

    <Style Selector="^:disabled">
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="{DynamicResource ListViewItemDisabledThemeOpacity}" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Rectangle#NormalRectangle">
        <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="{DynamicResource CheckBoxDisabledBorderThemeBrush}" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Path#CheckGlyph">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource CheckBoxDisabledForegroundThemeBrush}" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#SelectedBorder">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Path#SelectedEarmark">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="Transparent" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Path#SelectedGlyph">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="Transparent" />
      </Style>
    </Style>
  </ControlTheme>

  <!--
    The Windows Phone 8.1 GridView and GridViewItem: the 8.1 Update 1 runtime's gridview.json and gridviewitem.json (the
    SDK's generic.xaml), re-expressed as Avalonia ControlThemes on Avalonia's ListBox and ListBoxItem.
    docs/controls/GridView/PLAN.md has the values and their sources.

    In this file, not one of their own, as each is BasedOn the ListView's theme by StaticResource, which finds only a
    resource of its own file. Keyed, not by type, as the ListBox's (Controls/ListBox.axaml): Avalonia's ListBox already
    wears the ListView's look. The phone's GridView is a ListViewBase with a wrapping panel, and its item's template is
    the ListViewItem's, so both themes are based on the ListView's and change only what the phone's styles change. An app
    names the list; the list's theme gives its items theirs:

      <ListBox Theme="{DynamicResource Wp81GridViewTheme}" />
      <ListBoxItem Theme="{DynamicResource Wp81GridViewItemTheme}" />   (an item on its own)

    GridView: the ListView's, its template, its ScrollViewer's values and its check mode (SelectionMode Multiple with
    Toggle sets PhoneListMultiSelect.IsOn, which the items inherit), with the phone's ItemsWrapGrid, Orientation
    Horizontal, as Avalonia's WrapPanel: items fill a row left to right and wrap, and the list scrolls down.

    GridViewItem: the ListViewItem's template, press (Tilt on TiltContainer) and states, with GridViewItemMargin (0) and
    the content centred both ways (the phone's style sets neither alignment, so WinRT's Center stands, where the
    ListViewItem's sets Left and Top). Its check mode is GridMultiSelect, not ListMultiSelect: SelectedBorder, the 2.5
    accent border, on every item, and SelectedCheckMark, the earmark and its tick, on a selected one (the ListViewItem's
    :selected). The check box never comes in and the content doesn't move, so the box is hidden: never laid out, it has no
    bounds, so PhoneListMultiSelect finds no box to press, and a press anywhere on the item is its content's tilt.
  -->

  <ControlTheme x:Key="Wp81GridViewItemTheme" TargetType="ListBoxItem" BasedOn="{StaticResource {x:Type ListBoxItem}}">
    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="{DynamicResource GridViewItemMargin}" />
    <!-- Not set by the phone's style: WinRT's own default. -->
    <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
    <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />

    <!-- The ListMultiSelect box never comes in a GridView: hidden, so it neither draws nor takes the box's press. -->
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#CheckboxTiltContainer">
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
    </Style>

    <!-- GridMultiSelect: the border on every item; the content stays where it is. -->
    <Style Selector="^[(wp81|PhoneListMultiSelect.IsOn)=True]">
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#ContentBorder">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none" />
      </Style>
      <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#SelectedBorder">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1" />
      </Style>
    </Style>
  </ControlTheme>

  <ControlTheme x:Key="Wp81GridViewTheme" TargetType="ListBox" BasedOn="{StaticResource {x:Type ListBox}}">
    <Setter Property="ItemContainerTheme" Value="{DynamicResource Wp81GridViewItemTheme}" />
    <Setter Property="ItemsPanel">
      <ItemsPanelTemplate>
        <WrapPanel Orientation="Horizontal" />
      </ItemsPanelTemplate>
    </Setter>
  </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
